# Keep secrets, local state, and bulk out of the build context.
#
# Without this file, `COPY . .` bakes .env (Django secret key, R2 credentials,
# Anthropic API key) into an image layer, where it survives any later deletion
# and is readable by anyone who can pull the image.
#
# Runtime still gets .env: compose bind-mounts the project at /app, and the
# systemd deploy reads /opt/agrisynthia/.env directly.

# Secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# VCS and tooling
.git
.gitignore
.dockerignore
.pytest_cache/

# Root-level docs. Nothing at runtime reads them, and Docker patterns are not
# recursive, so this matches only the context root and leaves app-level
# markdown alone.
*.md

# Python bytecode and virtualenvs.
# Docker patterns are not implicitly recursive the way .gitignore is, so these
# need explicit ** to match at any depth.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
venv/
.venv/
env/

# Local runtime state, all provided by volumes at runtime
db.sqlite3
logs/
media/
staticfiles/
celerybeat-schedule
celerybeat-schedule.*

# Model weights are large and mounted via models_volume at runtime.
# Root-only on purpose: a bare "models/" in Docker matches only the top-level
# directory, so the vendored detection/yolo/models package is NOT excluded.
# It must stay, since predict_tree.py imports models.experimental from it.
/models
**/*.pt

# Not needed inside the image
deploy/
docs/
ssl/
monitoring/
reports/load*
scripts/_sample.jpg
